1. Identify basic necessary conditions for system operation:
   - Controller C must be operational; if C fails, the system fails.
   - At least two of the three sensors must succeed; equivalently, the system fails if at least two sensors fail.
   - At least one pump (including its support stream) must be available; equivalently, the system fails if both pumps are unavailable.

2. Express sensor failure condition:
   - "At least two sensors fail" = (S1 AND S2) OR (S1 AND S3) OR (S2 AND S3).

3. Express pump unavailability condition:
   - For pump i, the pump is unavailable if the pump device Pi fails OR its support stream Ai fails. So pump i failure event = (Pi OR Ai).
   - "Both pumps unavailable" = (P1 OR A1) AND (P2 OR A2).

4. Combine controller, sensor, and pump conditions into the top event:
   - Top event T occurs if controller fails OR sensor-failure condition OR both-pumps-unavailable condition. Thus:
     T = C OR [(S1 AND S2) OR (S1 AND S3) OR (S2 AND S3)] OR [(P1 OR A1) AND (P2 OR A2)]

5. Derive minimal cut sets (MCS). Minimal cut sets are minimal combinations of basic component failures that cause T:
   - Controller single failure:
     MCS1: {C}
   - Any two sensors failing:
     MCS2: {S1, S2}
     MCS3: {S1, S3}
     MCS4: {S2, S3}
   - Both pumps unavailable; expand (P1 OR A1) AND (P2 OR A2) into minimal pairs:
