Define events:
- A = "head occurs first" = {HH, HT}
- B = "exactly one head and one tail occur" = {HT, TH}

Compute probabilities (each of the 4 outcomes is equally likely, probability 1/4):
- P(B) = P(HT) + P(TH) = 1/4 + 1/4 = 1/2
- A ∩ B = {HT}
- P(A ∩ B) = P(HT) = 1/4

Apply conditional probability:
P(A|B) = P(A ∩ B) / P(B) = (1/4) / (1/2) = 1/2

P(Z ≤ z) = P(X + Y ≤ z) = ∫_{x=0}^{z} ∫_{y=0}^{z-x} f_X(x) f_Y(y) dy dx
= ∫_{0}^{z} ∫_{0}^{z-x} (λ e^{-λ x})(λ e^{-λ y}) dy dx
Inner integral: ∫_{0}^{z-x} λ e^{-λ y} dy = 1 - e^{-λ (z-x)}
So
F_Z(z) = ∫_{0}^{z} λ e^{-λ x} [1 - e^{-λ (z-x)}] dx
= ∫_{0}^{z} λ e^{-λ x} dx - ∫_{0}^{z} λ e^{-λ x} e^{-λ (z-x)} dx
First term: ∫_{0}^{z} λ e^{-λ x} dx = 1 - e^{-λ z}
Second term: e^{-λ z} ∫_{0}^{z} λ dx = e^{-λ z} (λ z)
Thus
F_Z(z) = (1 - e^{-λ z}) - λ z e^{-λ z} = 1 - (1 + λ z) e^{-λ z}
Differentiate to get the density:
f_Z(z) = d/dz [1 - (1 + λ z) e^{-λ z}] = λ^2 z e^{-λ z}
